    "summary": "High‑energy Dark Star → MLB jam and tight second‑set flow",
    "blurb": "Features a soaring Dark Star → Playing In The Band sequence, crisp Jerry tone, and powerful Phil bombs. The second set maintains high intensity through Mind Left Body Jam, Morning Dew, and an inspired encore with Eyes Of The World and Stella Blue.",
    "review": "The October 19, 1973 Oklahoma City Fairgrounds Arena show finds the Dead striking a balance between raw power and delicate interplay. While the first set meanders—keyboard levels sit forward early on and songs like Tennessee Jed and Looks Like Rain feel flat—the band recovers with a punchy Don't Ease Me In that leads into a standout Playing In The Band. The second set erupts, launching from China Cat Sunflower > I Know You Rider straight into an unforgettable Dark Star that morphs into a marathon Mind Left Body Jam before bursting into a heartfelt Morning Dew. Jerry’s tone is crystal‑clear and his solo work on the Dark Star/MLB transition soars, while Phil delivers his trademark “bombs” and a bass solo that lifts the entire jam. The rhythm section—Billy’s extra‑limbed drumming and Mickey’s steady pulse—keeps the momentum relentless. The encore rounds out the night with luminous renditions of Eyes Of The World and Stella Blue, cementing this performance as one of the high points of the 1973 fall tour.",
